{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"default-entry","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default Entry"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/markdown"},{"type":"text","value":" re-exports the parser, inline parser, HTML renderer, and all shared public types."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  parseInline,\n  parseMarkdown,\n  renderBlock,\n  renderDocument,\n  renderHtml,\n  renderInline,\n  type MarkdownDocument,\n  type RenderOptions,\n} from '@tanstack/markdown'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parsing-exports","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parsing exports"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"parsemarkdown","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parseMarkdown"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function parseMarkdown(\n  markdown: string,\n  options?: ParseOptions,\n): MarkdownDocument","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parses a complete Markdown document. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./parser.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parser Reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"parseinline","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parseInline"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function parseInline(value: string, options?: ParseOptions): InlineNode[]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parses inline content without block parsing. It is useful inside custom extension parsers. Standalone calls do not perform document-level link-definition or footnote extraction unless the relevant parser state is supplied in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ParseOptions"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"html-exports","children":[{"type":"text","value":"HTML exports"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"renderhtml","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderHtml"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renders a source string or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MarkdownDocument"},{"type":"text","value":" to HTML."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"renderdocument","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderDocument"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renders a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MarkdownDocument"},{"type":"text","value":". It is a document-specific alias over "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderHtml"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"renderblock","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderBlock"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renders one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"BlockNode"},{"type":"text","value":" to HTML."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"renderinline","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderInline"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renders one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InlineNode"},{"type":"text","value":" to HTML."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signatures and rendering options are documented in the "},{"type":"link","href":"./html.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"HTML Reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-exports","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type exports"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default entry exports every AST node, parser context, render option, extension contract, and supporting definition from the "},{"type":"link","href":"./types.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Types Reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"default-entry","text":"Default Entry","level":1},{"id":"parsing-exports","text":"Parsing exports","level":2},{"id":"parsemarkdown","text":"parseMarkdown","level":3},{"id":"parseinline","text":"parseInline","level":3},{"id":"html-exports","text":"HTML exports","level":2},{"id":"renderhtml","text":"renderHtml","level":3},{"id":"renderdocument","text":"renderDocument","level":3},{"id":"renderblock","text":"renderBlock","level":3},{"id":"renderinline","text":"renderInline","level":3},{"id":"type-exports","text":"Type exports","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Default Entry\n\n`@tanstack/markdown` re-exports the parser, inline parser, HTML renderer, and all shared public types.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  parseInline,\n  parseMarkdown,\n  renderBlock,\n  renderDocument,\n  renderHtml,\n  renderInline,\n  type MarkdownDocument,\n  type RenderOptions,\n} from '@tanstack/markdown'\n```\n\n## Parsing exports\n\n### `parseMarkdown`\n\n```ts\nfunction parseMarkdown(\n  markdown: string,\n  options?: ParseOptions,\n): MarkdownDocument\n```\n\nParses a complete Markdown document. See the [Parser Reference](./parser.md).\n\n### `parseInline`\n\n```ts\nfunction parseInline(value: string, options?: ParseOptions): InlineNode[]\n```\n\nParses inline content without block parsing. It is useful inside custom extension parsers. Standalone calls do not perform document-level link-definition or footnote extraction unless the relevant parser state is supplied in `ParseOptions`.\n\n## HTML exports\n\n### `renderHtml`\n\nRenders a source string or `MarkdownDocument` to HTML.\n\n### `renderDocument`\n\nRenders a `MarkdownDocument`. It is a document-specific alias over `renderHtml`.\n\n### `renderBlock`\n\nRenders one `BlockNode` to HTML.\n\n### `renderInline`\n\nRenders one `InlineNode` to HTML.\n\nSignatures and rendering options are documented in the [HTML Reference](./html.md).\n\n## Type exports\n\nThe default entry exports every AST node, parser context, render option, extension contract, and supporting definition from the [Types Reference](./types.md).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Default Entry\n---\n\n# Default Entry\n\n`@tanstack/markdown` re-exports the parser, inline parser, HTML renderer, and all shared public types.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  parseInline,\n  parseMarkdown,\n  renderBlock,\n  renderDocument,\n  renderHtml,\n  renderInline,\n  type MarkdownDocument,\n  type RenderOptions,\n} from '@tanstack/markdown'\n```\n\n## Parsing exports\n\n### `parseMarkdown`\n\n```ts\nfunction parseMarkdown(\n  markdown: string,\n  options?: ParseOptions,\n): MarkdownDocument\n```\n\nParses a complete Markdown document. See the [Parser Reference](./parser.md).\n\n### `parseInline`\n\n```ts\nfunction parseInline(value: string, options?: ParseOptions): InlineNode[]\n```\n\nParses inline content without block parsing. It is useful inside custom extension parsers. Standalone calls do not perform document-level link-definition or footnote extraction unless the relevant parser state is supplied in `ParseOptions`.\n\n## HTML exports\n\n### `renderHtml`\n\nRenders a source string or `MarkdownDocument` to HTML.\n\n### `renderDocument`\n\nRenders a `MarkdownDocument`. It is a document-specific alias over `renderHtml`.\n\n### `renderBlock`\n\nRenders one `BlockNode` to HTML.\n\n### `renderInline`\n\nRenders one `InlineNode` to HTML.\n\nSignatures and rendering options are documented in the [HTML Reference](./html.md).\n\n## Type exports\n\nThe default entry exports every AST node, parser context, render option, extension contract, and supporting definition from the [Types Reference](./types.md).\n"}
